---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "@/lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Linda Mohamed brings over a decade of cloud and agile expertise together with a deep practice of juggling — at The Juggling Company, the two are the same craft."
>
  <article class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-12 px-4 py-16 md:grid-cols-[18rem_1fr] md:px-6">
    <aside>
      <img
        src="/images/IMG_9810.jpg"
        alt="Linda Mohamed"
        width="320"
        height="400"
        class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-2xl border border-[var(--color-border)] object-cover shadow-lg"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-3 text-sm">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-muted)]">Role</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 text-[var(--color-fg)]">{site.author.role}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-muted)]">Based in</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 text-[var(--color-fg)]">London, United Kingdom</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-muted)]">Email</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 text-[var(--color-fg)]">
            <a class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline" href={`mailto:${site.author.email}`}>{site.author.email}</a>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </aside>

    <div>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-muted)]">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-5xl">
        {site.author.name}
      </h1>

      <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-none">
        <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Linda Mohamed has spent over a decade in tech, specialising in cloud
          technologies, IT process optimisation, and agile methodologies. She
          guides companies on cloud journeys, integrating cutting-edge
          technology with effective management practices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside her professional work, she has a deep passion for juggling
          — a skill that teaches balance, focus, and adaptability. The Juggling
          Company merges the art of juggling with innovative learning and
          development strategies.
        </p>

        <h2>Mission</h2>
        <p>
          At The Juggling Company, our mission is to inspire, educate, and
          empower individuals through the art of juggling. We are dedicated to
          fostering a vibrant community where juggling serves as a bridge
          between physical fitness, cognitive development, and creative
          expression. By integrating the principles of juggling with cutting-edge
          technology and innovative learning methods, we aim to promote
          holistic well-being, enhance teamwork, and drive positive change
          within organisations and individuals alike.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>One craft, two surfaces.</strong> Juggling and software both
            reward incremental load, fast feedback, and a calm response to
            dropped balls.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Bespoke before stock.</strong> Every keynote, workshop, and
            performance is tailored to the room — no recycled decks.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Evidence over vibe.</strong> The Ideas section cites the
            neuroscience the workshops draw on. The metaphor only earns its
            keep when the research holds.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
